WEBVTT

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.560
Is it really okay for me to borrow your bed?

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:11.150
Your furniture hasn't been delivered yet, so there's no choice.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.850
Or do you want to sleep together?

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.970
The sofa downstairs is fine for me too...

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.200
Are you stupid?

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:23.120
In what world do houses exist in which family members don't have places to sleep?

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:25.570
Don't be reserved.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:28.310
Okay.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:31.580
Well, I guess I'm going to sleep as well.

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:32.950
Hey.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.480
What is it?

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.270
It's about Kirino-chan...

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.350
Oh, about that.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.440
Don't worry about it.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.220
She'll still be walking to school together with us.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.100
<i>Passion</i>

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.100
But...

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.210
...is Kirino-chan really okay with that?

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.510
I kinda feel...

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.050
I was getting pretty spoiled by her as well.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.120
Things have simply returned to how they should be.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:01.610
At least I don't feel restraint about having you make me breakfast.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:03.450
What's that supposed to mean?

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.950
But it'll be okay like this, right?

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:09.110
Didn't you have that long ago as well?

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.890
I think its name was Sun, or Moon, or something...

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:13.110
Sunday!

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.550
Ah, right!

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:15.910
You're still carrying it around?

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:17.980
That's because it's important to me.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.960
Aren't you getting a little too old for stuffed animals?

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:23.750
It's all right.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.980
Because this is my...

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.400
...most important, most precious possession.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.720
Was it a present to you?

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.580
You couldn't have...

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:37.270
No, it's nothing.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:39.230
Good night.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.000
Good night, Onii-chan.

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:02.150
These feelings that I couldn't even tell my friends about

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:07.480
are still locked up inside me even now

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:12.570
If I eat the magical fruit inside my heart

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.540
they might actually be able to come out

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:23.150
I kept on waiting in the classroom

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:28.150
making excuses that it's just a coincidence

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:33.740
That smile is probably meant for someone

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:39.200
If dreams can make my wishes come true

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:44.150
I want to give you this present

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:49.320
I will transform your rainbow

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:54.280
into a bridge of happiness, just wave to me

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:59.560
It's all right, it's all right

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:04.910
I simply want to watch over you...

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:23.970
<i>The First Love</i>

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:24.470
Sorry for the wait.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.770
Ooh, this is curry pilaf!

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:29.200
Luxurious for a Sunday morning!

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.760
I found some red curry lying around.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:34.510
It's nearly past its expiration date though.

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:36.350
Because we never use it.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:40.620
Delicious!

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.950
Of course!

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.230
You're pretty skilled at cooking.

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:46.160
Unlike Kirino.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:47.950
Is that so?

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:54.070
After a period of trial and error, a harmless omelet became the dominant breakfast meal in our house.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.260
I see...

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.120
What are we doing today?

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:01.090
We're going shopping. Should we invite Kirino as well?

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:04.370
She said she had a meeting or something with the music club.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:07.030
She only just entered school and is already working hard.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:09.280
So she's still playing the piano...

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:11.540
She's been good at it since she was a child.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.010
She was always practicing...

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:15.380
What?

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:19.230
I was just thinking I hadn't seen her practice for a while now.

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:21.920
But then, it's not like I see her around the clock.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.580
<i>Narasaki Shopping District</i>

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:28.580
So heavy...

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:31.060
Why are you buying this much?

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.640
No complaining.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:35.210
They're all necessities of life.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.210
What I already have is fine, isn't it?

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.790
Just how are some fancy sofa covers and a doormat necessities?

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:45.410
The house simply lacks elegance.

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:48.250
An all-male household is so troublesome...

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:50.050
The practical over the aesthetic.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:52.260
Call it "Less is More."

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:55.270
And letting dust collect in the corner of the hallways?

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:57.860
A man needs to live with pride.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:59.330
<i>Note: "hokori" can mean both "dust" and "pride"</i>

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.600
You're mixing up words.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.460
By the way, shouldn't you be buying new furniture instead?

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:05.840
Some of your things that were delivered looked pretty ancient.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:06.740
No.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:07.490
Why?

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.530
Those are all things Dad bought for me in the past.

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:15.460
That's why I'm going to keep using them.

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:17.750
I see.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:19.450
Oh?

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:23.740
Amami-san and Riko-san!

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.120
Are you on a date?

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:27.620
How romantic.

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:29.210
No, you're wrong.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:30.850
If you will excuse me...

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:44.390
Riko-san, please come with me...

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:46.070
No, come with me.

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:48.880
Fukamine-san, if you will!

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:49.810
What is it?

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:51.590
What's up with you guys!?

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:54.450
I have no business with her brother, I wish you wouldn't disturb me.

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:55.310
Riko-san!

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:56.410
Please!

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.080
Riko-san!

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.240
Please wait!

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:00.290
Riko-san!

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:06.910
Hey...

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.830
Did I do something strange?

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:14.670
What are all those guys getting worked up about?

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:17.560
Good day, school idol and her brother.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:18.660
Idol?

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:19.650
Who?

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.330
What's this!?

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:26.050
That's from when we went shopping this Sunday!

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:29.540
A candid shot? That's pretty low.

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:33.940
However, thanks to this, Fukamine-san has become an idol overnight.

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:35.170
I see.

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:38.340
That's why everyone is swarming around her.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:40.310
It is especially because of her good looks.

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:42.500
There's no accounting for taste.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:46.130
Does that mean you don't find her attractive?

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:48.730
Well?

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:51.120
Why should I care!?

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.260
Onii-chan?

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:54.560
Riko-san!

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:12.670
Man...

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:15.760
Would you mind having lunch with me?

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:17.960
I made you a lunch.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:19.990
Err...

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:22.580
Hey!

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.380
You guys, cut it...

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:26.060
What do you want, Amami?

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:27.230
We're busy.

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:30.280
Please watch over us gently, dear Brother!

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:31.840
I'm not your brother!

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.310
I need to go to the bathroom.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:37.260
Riko-san!

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:48.110
It's not Riko's fault, but...

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.870
<i>Riko</i>

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:04.380
Onii-chan!

00:08:04.820 --> 00:08:06.000
Over here!

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.420
What are you sneaking around for?

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.180
Because those guys are so persistent.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:13.690
It's the only way we can eat together.

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:15.650
Then just eat together with those guys.

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:17.560
Are you serious?

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:18.320
Here.

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:19.600
Thanks.

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:27.820
Things have gotten kinda troublesome.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:28.900
I guess so.

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:31.200
What should I do...

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:34.260
It's all because of that picture.

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:36.690
It was made to look better than the real thing.

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:38.250
Who cares?

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.450
Isn't it nice to have so many people at your feet?

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:44.420
At my feet? You're saying that as if I'm enjoying this.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:45.920
That's not what I'm saying.

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:48.570
Where are you going?

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:50.670
I finished eating so I'm going back to the classroom.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:52.680
Won't you stay with me?

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:54.870
I'm not your bodyguard.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:57.300
I don't feel like being scorned by your fans.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:58.890
What's that supposed to mean?

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:01.470
You're acting hostile... I don't like it.

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:03.960
Oh really?

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:05.300
You're jealous.

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:19.950
Haruhiko-kun!

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:21.980
Haruhiko-kun?

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.200
Kirino?

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.830
What's wrong? You look upset.

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:30.280
Really!? You're just seeing things!

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:32.480
Riko-chan seems to be having a hard time.

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:34.540
Weren't you surprised!?

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:38.150
She suddenly became the school idol, isn't that hilarious!

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:41.390
I've seen the magazine as well.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.880
Riko-chan looked really cute in it.

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:47.150
She looked so blissful.

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:51.070
Maybe it's because she was able to come back to her precious brother's side?

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:55.240
The person who took it just had good skill.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:56.340
You think?

00:09:57.870 --> 00:09:59.810
Class 2-C?

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:03.350
Yeah, I hear she's really cute.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:06.480
Damn, every single one of them...

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:08.090
It's strange.

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:11.390
You're getting yourself so worked up over Riko.

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:13.450
As if you weren't siblings at all.

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:24.040
If we're not siblings... then what?

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:05.300
Riko?

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:12.840
Hey, Riko!

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:14.730
Riko!

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:20.490
Where did she go?

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:36.960
No, she hasn't come over. Did something happen to her?

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:39.420
<i>No, it's nothing. Sorry.</i>

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:41.790
Haruhiko-kun, are you outside right now?

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:43.790
<i>Yeah, for a bit. See you.</i>

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:52.930
Where did she go?

00:11:58.050 --> 00:11:58.870
Riko!?

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:01.590
It's you, Tama-nee...

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:03.020
I'm a bit busy right now...

00:12:12.050 --> 00:12:12.830
Riko!

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:16.010
Onii-chan...

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:18.200
Just what do you think you're doing?

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:20.690
I was searching for tomatoes.

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:22.100
Tomatoes?

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:24.190
They were sold out at the store...

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:27.680
I heard they grew them here, so I...

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.430
Oh, my.

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:32.520
Even Haruhiko-chan is soaked.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:33.850
Tama-nee...

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:38.270
Just when I was wondering who would visit in this kind of weather, it was Riko!

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:41.570
I was startled to see her there, soaking wet!

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:46.660
I'm sorry. I had no idea this was the research facility Tama-nee was working.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:49.590
Why would you come here for tomatoes in the first place!?

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:51.300
You wouldn't normally go out in this weather!

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:52.330
But...

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:55.370
Haruhiko-chan, don't raise your voice like that.

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:57.600
I'm sure she had her reasons.

00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:59.050
Even so...

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:03.870
Anyway, dry yourselves first. I'll go grab some towels.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:07.390
You two will catch a cold like that!

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:11.260
Onii-chan, tomatoes are your favorite food.

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:13.740
So I wanted them no matter what.

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:16.560
It didn't have to be today, did it?

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:21.110
But... it seemed you and me had gotten into a fight.

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:24.950
I just wanted to make things up with you...

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:26.900
Riko...

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:30.810
I'm sorry.

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:34.670
Idiot. We haven't been fighting.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:39.170
Don't make me worry like that, you idiot.

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:40.960
Getting yourself drenched like this...

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:42.710
Why do you keep calling me an idiot?

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.050
Because you are.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:46.140
You and me both.

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:50.970
I was at fault. I'm sorry, Riko.

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:54.440
You idiot...

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:01.670
37.8°C...

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:03.210
It figures.

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:04.220
Sorry.

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:05.350
Don't worry about it.

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:07.990
I'll make you some porridge later.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:09.240
You will?

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:10.250
You bet!

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:13.410
I'll feed you porridge boiled with passion!

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:15.460
Passion? What's that supposed to mean?

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:18.000
Well, it just means my cooking is love.

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:23.250
Well, see you later!

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:27.070
Onii-chan?

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:30.420
Having a cold can be nice as well.

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:32.640
You're being so nice to me.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:36.180
Idiot! You're blushing!

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:37.770
That's because of my fever.

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:47.220
How is Riko-chan doing?

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:49.620
She only has a slight fever now.

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:51.000
She's fine.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.050
Tama-nee came over as well.

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:54.450
Tama-neesan has?

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:55.370
Yeah.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.350
She said I could take the day off as well.

00:14:58.350 --> 00:15:01.970
But then Riko said that she preferred that I wasn't there since she also had to change and such.

00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:03.660
Well, that's natural.

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:07.930
We're siblings! There's no need for her to be that reserved.

00:15:07.930 --> 00:15:10.100
That's not really true.

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:11.040
Why not?

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:13.430
You're not related by blood.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:15.250
So?

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:17.740
So that means she's no different from me.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:19.180
In what way?

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:25.860
I'm saying that, if there had been a slight twist of fate...

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.790
...I might have been the one that was your little sister.

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:30.500
That's what I mean.

00:15:30.890 --> 00:15:33.590
So, say that you were my little sister.

00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:35.330
How would you want me to treat you?

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:38.710
I think I'd want you by my side.

00:15:39.970 --> 00:15:42.790
Then that means Riko was holding back after all.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:44.790
It's a bad habit of hers.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:46.790
It's because Riko-chan is kind.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:49.370
Then that means you're not?

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.220
Maybe so...

00:15:58.260 --> 00:15:59.680
Well, it's probably that.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:01.130
That?

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:05.760
People aren't capable of being lenient when it comes to romance.

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:09.060
You're as clueless as ever.

00:16:09.060 --> 00:16:11.370
But we're talking about Kirino here.

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:16.820
You haven't been looking very pleased yourself, watching your sister being chased by those guys.

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:20.700
It goes even more since there is no blood relation.

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:25.600
Think of her as your sister all you want, but from a biological viewpoint you are just a man and a woman.

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:28.000
Romantic feelings develop.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:42.200
It's me. Can I come in?

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:43.690
W-Wait a second!

00:16:44.510 --> 00:16:45.440
Come in.

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:48.320
How are you feeling?

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:50.200
I'm fine now.

00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:52.960
I was just about to get out of bed.

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:54.240
Let me see.

00:16:56.630 --> 00:16:58.880
Your fever seems to be gone.

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:00.480
That's what I was saying.

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:01.680
Good.

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:04.050
Maybe your porridge did the trick.

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:05.870
Let's leave it at that.

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:16.510
Riko...

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:27.490
Sorry!

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:36.200
It's from Kirino-chan. It says, "How are you feeling?"

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:37.690
I-I see...

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:43.310
There was a call for you from the publisher of that magazine earlier.

00:17:43.310 --> 00:17:45.560
They wanted to interview you.

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:46.730
Interview?

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:48.750
I don't really mind.

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:51.840
I guess I could make up some spicy stories for them.

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:52.880
Okay.

00:17:54.230 --> 00:17:55.470
Hey, Riko...

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:57.590
Just now...

00:17:58.060 --> 00:17:59.090
What?

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:02.010
No, it's nothing!

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:16.440
Your picture spawned a large amount of reactions from boys.

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:19.730
May I ask you questions about romance?

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:20.910
Sure.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.250
Well then, when did you experience your first love?

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:26.330
I think it was in... third grade.

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:30.500
Third grade?

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:32.690
<i>Thinking about it...</i>

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:35.740
<i>...that was my...</i>

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:41.750
I see.

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:44.800
So what came of it between you and that boy?

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:46.340
Nothing at all.

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:47.670
Because...

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:48.450
Because?

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:53.460
No, it's nothing.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:59.190
Things rarely work out with your first love.

00:19:00.310 --> 00:19:01.780
Then, to conclude.

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:05.280
Are you seeing someone right now, or if not, are you in love with someone?

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:10.220
Of course, you don't need to comment if it's too hard to answer.

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:13.600
I'm not seeing anyone.

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:17.480
However, there is someone I'm in love with.

00:19:27.170 --> 00:19:29.100
<i>It couldn't be that Riko also...</i>

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.570
Who would that be?

00:19:30.570 --> 00:19:33.610
If it is not too much trouble, could you tell me?

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:36.600
I'm in love with my first love, even now.

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:44.610
That surprised me.

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:47.700
About your first love.

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:50.120
I never thought you'd answer that.

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.670
Oh, that.

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:54.080
Third grade, huh?

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:56.620
That's right about when we met.

00:19:57.730 --> 00:19:58.840
That was...

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:00.940
I was just making things a little interesting for them.

00:20:01.580 --> 00:20:03.770
I think I kept it fairly tame.

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:05.440
So that was a lie...?

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:07.810
Of course it was.

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:08.940
I see...

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:13.020
Then I guess it's different from me.

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:18.030
I could answer that question in the same way.

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:19.820
Your first love?

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:22.710
It happened in third grade.

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:25.640
And I'm in love with that girl even now.

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:29.830
This is no lie or anything I made up.

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:33.170
Who do you think it is?

00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:48.180
My first love...

00:20:50.590 --> 00:20:51.680
...was you.

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:54.350
It was you, Riko.

00:20:57.420 --> 00:21:00.390
That story wasn't really just something you made up, was it?

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:03.210
What about you, Riko?

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:06.200
I...

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:14.020
But... Kirino-chan...

00:21:14.020 --> 00:21:14.850
Kirino?

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:17.190
I broke our promise...

00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:18.340
What are you talking about?

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:22.400
Riko?

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:23.920
I'm sorry...

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:26.550
So that's your answer...

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:28.140
I'm sorry...

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:32.420
You don't need to apologize!

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:34.100
I'm sorry...

00:21:35.530 --> 00:21:38.190
No, I should be apologizing.

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:41.970
Can I go back in?

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:43.320
Sure.

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:53.250
I got rejected, huh...

00:22:14.030 --> 00:22:18.210
In a corner of the classroom

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:24.800
I hummed my favourite song

00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:30.730
Why did those melancholic feelings

00:22:31.770 --> 00:22:34.960
well up within me today

00:22:36.510 --> 00:22:42.000
When I return, will this town

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:45.790
gently welcome me back?

00:22:45.790 --> 00:22:49.980
Hey, I want to meet you

00:22:51.540 --> 00:22:57.100
In times you feel down, I wish you would tell me

00:22:57.100 --> 00:23:02.020
before you can no longer turn back

00:23:03.090 --> 00:23:05.970
Building a heartfelt rainbow together

00:23:05.970 --> 00:23:08.780
Say that I'm not alone

00:23:08.780 --> 00:23:14.870
So that my prayers may be heard

00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:37.220
It is a bit sudden, but summer has come to Narasaki.

00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:41.790
This is part of the Gift's power, nothing to be surprised about.

00:23:42.310 --> 00:23:47.780
We have come to do expected things like seabathing...

00:23:47.780 --> 00:23:51.570
...however, there seems to be some unrest between Amami-san and Riko-san.

00:23:51.860 --> 00:24:01.830
<i>The Passing Summer</i>

00:23:52.070 --> 00:23:53.730
What could have happened?

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:56.990
Next time, "The Passing Summer."

00:23:57.650 --> 00:24:01.100
Who will you give your Gift?
